# Copy to hooks/commit-size.conf to change the staged-size ceiling of git-hooks/pre-commit.
# LIMIT_MB is the most the files of ONE commit may total, in megabytes. No file, or a value
# that is not a positive whole number, means the built-in default: 10.
# A deliberate bigger commit: `SIZE_OK=1 git commit ...` (logged in the override ledger; refused
# if the ledger line cannot be written).
LIMIT_MB=10
